    "title": "A guide to celebrating New Year's Eve in Tempe - NewsBreak",
    "text": "14 hours ago\nAll Tempe municipal buildings and courts are closed Jan. 1 in observance of the New Year's holiday.\nOn Dec. 31, light rail/Streetcar service will be extended until 2 a.m. Bus, rail and paratransit services will be free Valley-wide starting at 7 p.m., courtesy of Coors Light Free Rides. Orbit service will be enhanced to operate as needed from the Tempe Transit Center until 2 a.m. on Jan. 1.\nIn accordance with state law the use of fireworks is permitted by Arizona law through Jan. 4 until 11 p.m. each night, except for New Year’s Eve when they are allowed until 1 a.m. The City of Tempe cannot change this law.",
